node_modules

# The mock fixtures under mocks/ are self-contained projects with their
# own formatter (see e.g. mocks/tsuzuri/package.json) and their own
# conventions — reformatting them to this repository's house style would
# diverge them from what their own toolchain expects, so this repository's
# gates never cover them; the mock's own toolchain is what keeps it honest.
mocks

# An evaluation's derived layer is regenerated and then compared BYTE FOR BYTE
# against what is committed, which is how a hand-edited summary is caught (see
# tools/effect-eval/summarize.mjs --check). Those bytes come from exactly one
# serializer — layout.mjs's `canonicalJson` — so a second formatter with an
# opinion about them would make the drift check fail against a file the
# instrument never wrote. The measured files under measurements/ are excluded
# for the plainer reason that nothing here authored them.
#
# Deliberately NOT the whole of data/: README.md and fixture.json are ordinary
# hand-written files and stay covered.
data/*/measurements/
data/*/summary.json
